PrimMST(G, V)
Input: Weighted connected graph G, No. of vertices V
Output: Minimum Spanning Tree and Total Cost

Step 1: Start
Step 2: Create array key[V] = {INF}, parent[V] = {-1}, mstSet[V] = {false}
Step 3: Set key[0] = 0
Step 4: For count = 0 to V-1 do:
        a) Find vertex u with minimum key[u] such that mstSet[u] == false
        b) Set mstSet[u] = true
        c) For each vertex v from 0 to V-1:
           If adjMatrix[u][v] != 0 AND mstSet[v] == false 
           AND adjMatrix[u][v] < key[v] then
              parent[v] = u
              key[v] = adjMatrix[u][v]
Step 5: Display edges: parent[i] - i for i=1 to V-1
Step 6: Calculate TotalCost = sum of key[i] for i=1 to V-1
Step 7: Display TotalCost
Step 8: Stop
